#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119619 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "d5a81b39-421e-55c3-90de-d9f4e6489cd5" :question/math-academy-id "e-4795" :question/problem "Determine if $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\},$ where\n![](images/3c/3c308ca93d8a6fa7ac5c6a037fa3f0a409d7253513db04922cc622750e230691.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=8 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = 3,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\mathbf{b}$ does *not* lie in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119620 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "94a17888-dcef-58e0-8147-0dec3745f136" :question/math-academy-id "e-4799" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $\\mathbf{u}$ lies on the plane $\\;\\Pi \\,:\\, \\mathbf{r}=s \\mathbf{b} + t \\mathbf{c}, \\, t,s \\in \\mathbb{R},$ where  $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 1, 4, 5 \\rangle, \\mathbf{c} = \\langle 2, 4, 6 \\rangle$ and  $\\mathbf{u}= \\langle 2, 10, 12 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $\\mathbf{u} \\in \\Pi$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 10 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+2t &=2 \\\\ 4s+4t &=10 \\\\ 5s+6t &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+2t &=2 \\\\ -4t &=2 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-4t = 2 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad t = -\\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s+2t & =2 \\\\ s+2(-\\frac{1}{2}) & =2 \\\\ s-1 & =2 \\\\ s & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=3, \\, t=-\\dfrac{1}{2},$ we conclude that $\\mathbf{u}$ does indeed lie on the plane $\\Pi.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u}=3\\mathbf{b} - \\dfrac{1}{2}\\mathbf{c}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119671 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/id #uuid "21a6808a-5b1c-5b1d-9bd4-da605fb6d920" :question/math-academy-id "e-6218" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a}_1, \\mathbf{a}_2 \\},$ where\n![](images/a5/a5ce805c69da0bd2e941aa56a9781ed430c8f0ce7b646bf2a6ea04168ee10cda.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}13 \\\\ -5 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=13 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2} &=-5 \\\\ 7{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 5 & 4 & -5 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 7 & 2 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 14 & -70 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{14}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 16 & k-91\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-16{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 13 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-11\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = k-11$. Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0 = k-11 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad k=11.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563732 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1442cd36-01ab-57b5-b752-7b7131e887f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562987} {:answer/id #uuid "1f1cbd99-3722-58a8-94e3-9b80df51c48b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563016} {:answer/id #uuid "38fb4394-142f-596a-acba-652af141f7ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563073} {:answer/id #uuid "976c158b-03de-5101-af86-c772a635e855" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563285} {:answer/id #uuid "98c56786-6605-5401-b672-c63cb1cecd33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98c56786-6605-5401-b672-c63cb1cecd33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563288} :answer-field/id #uuid "7847d689-0e36-5ac4-b435-bd1cf0642bc0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563577}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c391d9c3-0c76-5e6f-b0c3-d6b4ee2c37cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-105199" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=3 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+2{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=3\\cdot 2=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563678 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05a3b4f0-37fc-510b-b782-70713c302e3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562949} {:answer/id #uuid "0e4b9832-4e75-5456-ae0f-c9cbef897a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562972} {:answer/id #uuid "79384773-3b33-5558-b1a4-01487217122d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563212} {:answer/id #uuid "d55768be-caa1-5015-a0a0-51da48688614" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563412} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b9c506-0e84-558b-99e5-7b80605f2397" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e4b9832-4e75-5456-ae0f-c9cbef897a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562972} :answer-field/id #uuid "a41c8e29-8919-560f-acd3-bb2401f756f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563609}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "435bef4b-b3af-5768-973e-b4aa50ac129d" :question/math-academy-id "q-105235" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ k\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-9{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+10{x}_{2}=k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -9 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 10 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 10 & k\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k-6\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k-6.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k-6\\,⇒\\,k=6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "351d3eaa-8d71-5eaf-91f1-6a15d982842b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238515} {:answer/id #uuid "521c8347-9356-57c0-82a2-f6f058e2fdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238763} {:answer/id #uuid "77e423df-6336-5ebd-a988-70ffd97ff91b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239089} {:answer/id #uuid "9e933237-ff23-52d2-a25d-7ee910ab795d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239441} {:answer/id #uuid "b70c1cd0-e286-53f1-ba39-4e8669a377a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "521c8347-9356-57c0-82a2-f6f058e2fdd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238763} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca08aa7d-69a4-53e7-9a42-33232fc442bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240683}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "847914f8-60db-55a2-9155-7cfe231e6bcb" :question/math-academy-id "q-105237" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{2} &=-6 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+12{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 12 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+9\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+9.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+9\\,⇒\\,k=-9.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18da01e3-a753-5c12-b310-e49dbac1352a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421499} {:answer/id #uuid "8b330e4c-1039-5eb3-95e3-86ecad96d372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421510} {:answer/id #uuid "94545aa5-65f2-555f-8c83-9dc00de7552e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421512} {:answer/id #uuid "c506c166-ea56-5484-9ce8-55f2a4ef6b2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421516} {:answer/id #uuid "d5866e44-8aa4-58d9-b2ef-ad9461dd3c47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b330e4c-1039-5eb3-95e3-86ecad96d372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421510} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e5fe0f3-2bfd-5489-af0f-1a776954c9bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421526}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cdba03e5-45ad-5856-b84f-f9bccefe0c86" :question/math-academy-id "q-105242" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 39\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 39\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -6 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+7{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+18{x}_{2} &=-6 \\\\ 5{x}_{1}+39{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 18 & -6 \\\\ 5 & 39 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 39 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k+15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4 & k+15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-4){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+19\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+19.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+19\\,⇒\\,k=-19.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241023 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "202fca4b-d4db-559c-86f9-155db3d13c64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238333} {:answer/id #uuid "2b56c1db-87eb-5ec9-914d-30a522b26fe5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238442} {:answer/id #uuid "6182bb36-df22-5b55-8de2-18be6f4e6edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238911} {:answer/id #uuid "a846d2c7-f2b2-52b6-aa5d-db3effda179c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239517} {:answer/id #uuid "f503a4ab-d69a-5e93-a2e0-b67020545fa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6182bb36-df22-5b55-8de2-18be6f4e6edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238911} :answer-field/id #uuid "13f36fa9-d65b-5d54-8f7f-9bbf30419197" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "caedc8c2-ba3c-5e61-ad1f-0d5eafbb8652" :question/math-academy-id "q-105257" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,-2,-1⟩$, $c=⟨-4,5,-1⟩$, and  $u=⟨1,1,4⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-4t &=1 \\\\ -2s+5t &=1 \\\\ -s-t &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s-4t &=1 \\\\ t &=-1 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\nt=-1.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s-4t & =1 \\\\ s-4(-1) & =1 \\\\ s+4 & =1 \\\\ s & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=-3,\\,t=-1,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=-3b-c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=(-3)\\cdot (-1)=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314972 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "077cc4da-3c12-5749-87e3-9136fa56ff18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312025} {:answer/id #uuid "39d686df-f396-5c82-92b8-3b075c274d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312445} {:answer/id #uuid "4dd5ec6b-997e-5c4c-82cd-f74e85dcbdf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312607} {:answer/id #uuid "7578cf04-a90c-5b5d-ac09-511fd3e57a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312909} {:answer/id #uuid "2efb3d59-10d0-57b0-b6f6-06c1b609ee7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186422770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7578cf04-a90c-5b5d-ac09-511fd3e57a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312909} :answer-field/id #uuid "901fd7a3-f614-5740-8413-9326f82935f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314396}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dffa9b37-7313-5190-ae5f-372cf9f5aaea" :question/math-academy-id "q-34058" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-1=1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot 1=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563719 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e4a4287-0b4e-5134-b26d-e720107fbfce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563012} {:answer/id #uuid "32966283-95f9-59c0-9da8-620246a44c9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563060} {:answer/id #uuid "35881d2a-16d1-5e15-a12f-b325e9f8db16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563066} {:answer/id #uuid "4d4a40a4-8887-524e-8b48-8a24128d12fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563117} {:answer/id #uuid "d639618d-a932-5b03-8225-fae8a0b21ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563414}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35881d2a-16d1-5e15-a12f-b325e9f8db16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563066} :answer-field/id #uuid "283164aa-73de-5dcd-8a69-e6c9e6374abc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563546}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a8427e64-b547-5ecb-a62e-824aa188b632" :question/math-academy-id "q-34114" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}=-1 \\\\ 0=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}_{1}+(-1){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 2\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]+(-1)\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=2\\cdot (-1)=-2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0df36293-7642-519e-989b-c1e17518df82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315203} {:answer/id #uuid "237940e7-5e66-5e04-810d-4352d61a17a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315314} {:answer/id #uuid "8d7d7960-d998-5521-90f4-d62f2e5dcd41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315910} {:answer/id #uuid "b6f90b4d-fc27-5736-8b5c-3292c7be6212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316157} {:answer/id #uuid "dc225773-7e3f-55f2-b9a4-b3e9cdcb7d3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0df36293-7642-519e-989b-c1e17518df82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186315203} :answer-field/id #uuid "9edde81d-d00d-5468-9796-d7ae23f5cfcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d12a13d-137e-5159-9c9a-8fb99c09543c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34205" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -4{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=-6 \\\\ -7{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2} &=-11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -3 & -6 \\\\ -7 & -5 & -11\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ -7 & -5 & -11\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+7{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -18\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 9 & -18\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-9{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-2.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+2(-2)=-1\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=3.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{a}_{1}+(-2){a}_{2} & =b \\\\ 3\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}+(-2)\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -11\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}=3\\cdot (-2)=-6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3e187ae-ec73-5aa1-9abb-af1c37a04e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117964} {:answer/id #uuid "f599967e-0d55-5000-8d08-18e8b2019415" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117965} {:answer/id #uuid "3f96ba47-3040-5cc5-86c1-c15ce4efec90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117966} {:answer/id #uuid "439eec06-2d3c-58c3-bad8-9890bad26667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117967} {:answer/id #uuid "63dd41e5-a3ae-56ec-a457-dcd105edbda0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117968}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3e187ae-ec73-5aa1-9abb-af1c37a04e5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117964} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f43defc-60eb-5fef-a664-a3e6a18cbfdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117963}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cc1044df-5089-5bf6-ad79-aebf9c199eb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-34207" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,5,8⟩$, $c=⟨-1,-1,-3⟩$, and  $u=⟨-3,5,-7⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}s-t=-3 \\\\ 5s-t=5 \\\\ 8s-3t=-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 8 & -3 & -7\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-8{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 20 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 17\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-5{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-8,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119808 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "012982fc-c0c6-5360-983d-5c24ecfa5a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "162" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562940} {:answer/id #uuid "3ef56e44-9e80-5352-bfb2-5d35c8c19329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563087} {:answer/id #uuid "65e52e96-8639-5303-a9f5-06fb2d4d391c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "54" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563179} {:answer/id #uuid "84afc469-3802-566a-b03f-b05bcd3fd37e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563242} {:answer/id #uuid "bcb4217f-2b11-5476-8d7f-3c0e1e75e42b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "012982fc-c0c6-5360-983d-5c24ecfa5a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "162" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562940} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d94e257-45da-5352-bd7b-f0680253dc5b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563523}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ddfb229d-f01d-542c-8a6c-f2e9a5996154" :question/math-academy-id "q-34639" :question/problem "The vectors ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$, ${a}_{3}$, and $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}$ from the decomposition $b={x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}.$\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$, ${x}_{2}$ and ${x}_{3}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=3 \\\\ 4{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=18 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{3}=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -8 & 18 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=3 \\\\ {x}_{2}=6 \\\\ {x}_{3}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=3.$ Substituting into the first equation gives \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-2(3)=3\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=9.\n$$\n\nSince the system has a solution, we can conclude that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}\\}.$\n\nMoreover, there is exactly one solution, so we have exactly one way to write $b$ as a linear combination of ${a}_{1}$, ${a}_{2}$ and ${a}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{a}_{1}+6{a}_{2}+3{a}_{3} & =b \\\\ 9\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+6\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}\\cdot {x}_{3}=9\\cdot 6\\cdot 3=162.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342230 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04ad9e02-0e28-5883-8383-80771f092ba1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339164} {:answer/id #uuid "429c3c68-2ae7-53e0-b37e-d3c96ecd5672" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339712} {:answer/id #uuid "7407de37-953c-52c3-9691-7a1948812671" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340155} {:answer/id #uuid "9c61980b-b3a4-5a5c-866f-cfae9f4280c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340538} {:answer/id #uuid "ff51d081-de5e-5605-93dc-c11008dd57a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c61980b-b3a4-5a5c-866f-cfae9f4280c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340538} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf553037-64a2-590c-b4fb-05bae9f5c8de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cef0a842-c20f-55db-9989-525f1aca72a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-74558" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-5{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\nk=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342238 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "fac58a79-2d3f-5ad3-b1ab-c5ce279c4ebe" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Value of an Unknown Such That a Vector Lies in the Span of Given Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dc6fae0-6fc8-5ce6-8524-68dfcc8dcd8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340263} {:answer/id #uuid "d804a124-1946-56c4-a682-7985f9351701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341044} {:answer/id #uuid "eabc7ef9-665b-5387-a4c7-5e2ca3d36188" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341200} {:answer/id #uuid "eec7a1c7-8ad3-5a27-876f-0162e54d2cdb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341235} {:answer/id #uuid "f54514a3-c908-5fb8-b5c9-a864f0c8a55b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "90" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341290}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d804a124-1946-56c4-a682-7985f9351701" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341044} :answer-field/id #uuid "c44d1be5-bc0f-5bba-aed3-5e89db45d7c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341722}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "329f79c0-9230-5c7a-8435-3cce24f63578" :question/math-academy-id "q-74596" :question/problem "Find the values of $k$ such that the vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $b\\in \\text{Span}{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}}$ if there exist ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2} & =b \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 10\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -12\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -9 \\\\ k\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2} &=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=-9 \\\\ 10{x}_{1}-12{x}_{2} &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 10 & -12 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 6 & -8 & -3 \\\\ 10 & -12 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -30 \\\\ 10 & -12 & k\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+5{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -30 \\\\ 0 & 3 & k-45\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -30 \\\\ 0 & 0 & k+45\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=k+45.$ Therefore, the system has a solution only if\n\n$$\n0=k+45\\,⟹\\,k=-45.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342241 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2486b2f1-5c38-55cd-a205-21e202e09c4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339446} {:answer/id #uuid "2cadd916-ed59-5b50-9446-268229ac2732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339516} {:answer/id #uuid "4cc45ccf-adc7-53ad-a852-af95cfc40061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339825} {:answer/id #uuid "733ba44c-1a53-5f59-af78-2d354dda43f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340150} {:answer/id #uuid "7caedebc-c212-5602-b507-20831a0f0c1f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340251}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2cadd916-ed59-5b50-9446-268229ac2732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339516} :answer-field/id #uuid "520ff562-4653-55df-b4dc-8fbcaed97a63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d6c3f74b-5a27-519e-8d22-1736702759dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-74599" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨-1,4,3⟩$, $c=⟨1,-6,-7⟩$, and  $u=⟨1,-10,-15⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -6 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+t &=1 \\\\ 4s-6t &=-10 \\\\ 3s-7t &=-15\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -6 & -10 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -15\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -12\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-s+t &=1 \\\\ -2t &=-6 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n-2t=-6\\,⟹\\,t=3.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-s+t & =1 \\\\ -s+3 & =1 \\\\ -s & =-2 \\\\ s & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=2,\\,t=3,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=2b+3c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=2\\cdot 3=6.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186344944 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66b81663-6e80-51d7-a913-48b15173205e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343109} {:answer/id #uuid "8714c620-1893-528d-8182-61236ee13206" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343405} {:answer/id #uuid "b53eaae6-d50b-5fbe-95be-daf4107639c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343824} {:answer/id #uuid "ec48cbca-b54e-529c-a456-f0f5a7c0d8b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344311} {:answer/id #uuid "ef0d8fa3-1d8c-594e-b99a-40e3f03c6dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef0d8fa3-1d8c-594e-b99a-40e3f03c6dce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344340} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a27d35b-cc89-5818-8e8d-5ccf5c8819cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c8c4efc9-6266-5ebb-8bcb-7388b1494f8e" :question/math-academy-id "q-74605" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc,$ $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,3,6⟩$, $c=⟨1,-2,4⟩$, and  $u=⟨3,19,-10⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 19 \\\\ -10\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+t &=3 \\\\ 3s-2t &=19 \\\\ 6s+4t &=-10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 19 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 10 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -28\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -28\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -32\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}=-32,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $s$ and $t$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc=u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $u$ does *not* lie on the plane $Π.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186393417 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119809 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a04b551f-3323-5b91-b01e-941912cc92be" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Vector Lies on a Plane"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7eb8a46-2267-5072-8709-51251ce9e760" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393419} {:answer/id #uuid "4af5620d-a92f-5f04-b9d9-0982f3d2a131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393420} {:answer/id #uuid "9db239d2-39ff-503c-9288-54070e1b2d71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393421} {:answer/id #uuid "145d4992-30fd-5d3a-9dbb-d5d2652afc6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393422} {:answer/id #uuid "fbde74ee-e78a-57a1-9751-28a91866994f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$u$ does not lie on $Π$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9db239d2-39ff-503c-9288-54070e1b2d71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393421} :answer-field/id #uuid "b06e84e5-8b15-54ef-8727-430594345689" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186393418}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4018a53f-b299-52cf-a135-1013bf76ce32" :question/math-academy-id "q-74607" :question/problem "Determine if the vector $u$ lies on the plane $Π:r=sb+tc$, $t,s\\in R$, where  $b=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $c=⟨3,8,-7⟩$, and  $u=⟨9,22,-5⟩.$ In the affirmative case, find the value of $s\\cdot t$ from the decomposition $u=sb+tc.$" :question/worked-solution "By definition, $u\\in Π$ if there exist $t$ and $s$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}sb+tc & =u \\\\ s\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 22 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+3t &=9 \\\\ 2s+8t &=22 \\\\ 3s-7t &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 8 & 22 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -7 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -16 & -32\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}s+3t &=9 \\\\ 2t &=4 \\\\ 0 &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n2t=4\\,⟹\\,t=2.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s+3t & =9 \\\\ s+3(2) & =9 \\\\ s & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we found a solution $s=3,\\,t=2,$ we conclude that $u$ does indeed lie on the plane $Π.$ In fact, we have\n\n$$\nu=3b+2c.\n$$\n\nFinally, $s\\cdot t=3\\cdot 2=6.$"}]}
